---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navigation from '../components/Navigation.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const pillars = [
  {
    title: 'Computer science',
    text: "I came to code late — only after starting university — which means I still remember what it feels like not to understand it. That perspective keeps me grounded. When something breaks, the machine doesn't lie; it tells you exactly where your thinking went wrong, and that brutal honesty is liberating. The craft isn't in writing clever code. It's in building systems where each piece clicks into place and complexity resolves into clarity.",
  },
  {
    title: 'Poker',
    text: "I study GTO charts not to memorize them but to understand the reasoning beneath the ranges. That understanding is what gives you the freedom to deviate — because the real art isn't playing optimally, it's knowing when to bend the rules because your opponent isn't optimal either. Every fold is data. Every bet is a question. Every river card is a reminder that you control the decision, never the outcome.",
  },
  {
    title: 'Writing',
    text: "Writing is thinking made visible — the slow work of turning vague intuition into something sharp enough to cut. Wittgenstein believed the limits of language are the limits of our world, and I take that as a standing challenge: to find sentences that expand understanding rather than constrain it. I write to discover what I think, and occasionally the sentence that emerges is clearer than the thought that started it. That's when I know I'm onto something.",
  },
  {
    title: 'Basketball',
    text: "There's a bit of Kyrie in my step — quick, unpredictable, finding space where none seems to exist. What draws me to the game is its artistry: passes threaded through tight windows, cuts and shots so precise they feel like geometry come alive. The wordless communication is the best part, eyes meeting across the court, a subtle gesture that shifts the entire play. And yes, there's the moment when the shot drops and the crowd screams.",
  },
  {
    title: 'Gaming',
    text: "Whatever the genre, my approach is the same: understand the essence first. Before grinding for wins, I want to know why the system works the way it does. That understanding is the shortcut. The victories come quietly — not from loud triumphs but from watching the pattern emerge, from turning complexity into simplicity. No rage quits, no tilting; just the satisfaction of a plan unfolding as predicted, or the quick pivot when it doesn't.",
  },
];
---

<Layout title="About - Mingxi Yan" description="About Mingxi Yan — how I came to code late, and what I've been chasing since.">
  <Navigation />

  <main class="flex-grow">
    <!-- Header -->
    <section class="pt-16 pb-10 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 border-b border-gray-200">
      <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight mb-5 opacity-0 animate-fade-in-up">About</h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed font-serif opacity-0 animate-fade-in-up delay-100">
          I came to code late, and I have been making up for it ever since.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Origin -->
    <section class="py-14 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        <div class="space-y-5 text-gray-700 leading-[1.75] font-serif text-[1.0625rem]">
          <p>
            I wrote my first line of code after starting university. Everyone around me seemed to have
            been programming since they were twelve, and for a while that felt like a deficit I would
            never close.
          </p>
          <p>
            It turned out to be the opposite. Because I learned it late, I remember every place it was
            confusing, and I can still find my way back to not understanding something — which is most
            of what teaching is, and a fair amount of what good engineering is too. The best systems I
            have built were the ones I could explain to the version of me who did not get it yet.
          </p>
          <p>
            The rest of what I do follows the same shape. I invent poker games and then need a platform
            to run them. I read solver output and then want to know why it says what it says. I write
            to find out what I actually think. In every case the interesting part is not the answer —
            it is getting the system to explain itself.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Pillars -->
    <section class="py-14 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 bg-gray-50 border-y border-gray-200">
      <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="text-sm font-sans font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-gray-500 mb-8">What I spend time on</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-x-12 gap-y-10">
          {pillars.map(pillar => (
            <div class="border-t border-gray-300 pt-5">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold mb-3">{pillar.title}</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">{pillar.text}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- What I'm looking for -->
    <section class="py-14 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="text-sm font-sans font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-gray-500 mb-7">What I'm looking for</h2>
        <div class="space-y-5 text-gray-700 leading-[1.75]">
          <p>
            Work where the engineering is rigorous and the problem is worth solving — ideally at the
            point where AI systems meet actual people, since that is where the hard questions live.
          </p>
          <p>
            I am also looking for conversations. If you think about technology, game theory, or
            philosophy, I would like to talk. Most of my better ideas arrived through someone whose
            background looked nothing like mine.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- A few more things -->
    <section class="py-14 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 bg-gray-50 border-y border-gray-200">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="text-sm font-sans font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-gray-500 mb-7">A few more things</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-4 text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
          <li class="flex"><span class="text-gray-400 mr-3 shrink-0">—</span><span>I am convinced most complex problems can be solved with a whiteboard and enough time.</span></li>
          <li class="flex"><span class="text-gray-400 mr-3 shrink-0">—</span><span>Slow down. Even when the world rushes forward, the discoveries that matter happen in the quiet spaces where we let ourselves pause.</span></li>
          <li class="flex"><span class="text-gray-400 mr-3 shrink-0">—</span><span>Some things matter more to me than profit: the elegance of a solution, the depth of understanding, the effect on people's lives. This is not true when I am playing poker.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Closing philosophy -->
    <section class="py-16 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
        <div class="space-y-5 text-gray-700 leading-[1.75] font-serif text-[1.0625rem]">
          <p class="text-lg italic">"Be curious. Stay humble. Build things that matter."</p>
          <p>
            Freedom is not the absence of constraints but the willingness to be shaped by what you
            did not choose. To live fully is to hold the balance between the paths taken and the ones
            left behind — not as a conqueror of the world, but as a participant in it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Contact -->
    <section class="py-16 px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 bg-black text-white">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-8 text-center">Let's talk</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 text-center">
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold mb-2 text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-wide">Professional</h3>
            <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/mingxi-yan-0b9581272" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-gray-200 hover:text-white transition-colors">LinkedIn</a>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold mb-2 text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-wide">Code</h3>
            <a href="https://github.com/PittsIrv" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-gray-200 hover:text-white transition-colors">GitHub</a>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold mb-2 text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-wide">Direct</h3>
            <a href="mailto:mingxiy66@gmail.com" class="text-gray-200 hover:text-white transition-colors">Email</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-10 text-center text-gray-400 text-sm">
          Whether you want to discuss a project, share ideas, or just say hi — I am always happy to connect.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
